(1  | p | group) in both formulas ensures that the random intercepts of both model parts are modeled as correlated.

You could specify dat$group <- 1:nrow(dat) to have actual residuals, which is then modeled as correlated via | p |.

Your initial explanation sounds as if this is exactly what you want, but I might be wrong.

