From u3b26edfa43fe7a09 at groups.google.com  Thu Jan 18 12:52:11 2018
From: u3b26edfa43fe7a09 at groups.google.com (RV)
Date: Thu, 18 Jan 2018 12:52:11 +0000
Subject: Problem with LOO(x, reloo = TRUE)
Message-ID: <LnuAJ1sjSO4.PXH0LGSaAAAJ@brms-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/brms-users/c/LnuAJ1sjSO4/m/PXH0LGSaAAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I'm fitting a model (let's call it q) in which I have to set the inits argument to 0 to avoid problems with initialization like this:

Rejecting initial value:
  Log probability evaluates to log(0), i.e. negative infinity.
  Stan can't start sampling from this initial value.

After running LOO on the model it turned out that one parameter has a Pareto k value larger than 0.7. I have thus tried:

LOO(q, reloo = TRUE)

After this call I get the same error as above. Could it be that LOO doesn't take the inits argument into account?

From u6e3dd74b422c061b at groups.google.com  Thu Jan 18 13:11:25 2018
From: u6e3dd74b422c061b at groups.google.com (Paul Buerkner)
Date: Thu, 18 Jan 2018 13:11:25 +0000
Subject: Re: [brms-users] Problem with LOO(x, reloo = TRUE)
Message-ID: <LnuAJ1sjSO4.fZtWTQXOAAAJ@brms-users.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <LnuAJ1sjSO4.PXH0LGSaAAAJ@brms-users.groups.google.com>
References: <LnuAJ1sjSO4.PXH0LGSaAAAJ@brms-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/brms-users/c/LnuAJ1sjSO4/m/fZtWTQXOAAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

If reloo = TRUE, the model is fit multiple times each leaving out one of the problematic observations.

To set inits = 0 during refitting go for

LOO(q, reloo = TRUE, update_args = list(inits = 0))

